  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the caller in the emergency scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the man on the phone (man_on_phone) who is calling 911. This projection is implied by the meme's framing, where the viewer is positioned as the one making the call or as the one who would understand the absurdity of the situation. The text '911, what is your emergency?' and the visual of the man on the phone create a direct address to the viewer, inviting them to imagine themselves in the role of the caller. The user is not explicitly deictic (e.g., 'me' or 'you'), but the scene and text create an implicit identification with the caller, who is the central figure in the action.",
